{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_10f0fbc2bdc049418991807a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now the test files. First the stub helper file `pkg/scripts/stub_git_test.go`.\n\nThen `pkg/scripts/repo_clone_test.go`.\n\nLet me write the stub helper file.\n\nLicense header needed for .go files (addlicense adds it). Let me include it.\n\nstub_git_test.go content:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n\npackage scripts_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n)\n\n// repoCloneStubGitScript is a stand-in for git on PATH.\n//\n// It logs every invocation, and for `clone` it creates the destination and a\n// per-call marker file, so a spec can tell a first clone from a second one.\nconst repoCloneStubGitScript = `#!/usr/bin/env bash\necho \"$*\" >> \"$STUB_GIT_LOG\"\nif [ \"$1\" = \"clone\" ]; then\n  for last in \"$@\"; do :; done\n  mkdir -p \"$last\"\n  index=\"$(grep -c '^clone ' \"$STUB_GIT_LOG\")\"\n  echo marker > \"$last/stub-clone-marker-$index\"\n  if [ -n \"$STUB_GIT_LINK_TARGET\" ]; then\n    ln -s \"$STUB_GIT_LINK_TARGET\" \"$last/link\"\n  fi\n  exit \"${STUB_GIT_CLONE_EXIT:-0}\"\nfi\nexit 0\n`\n\n// repoCloneWriteStubGit installs the stub as `git` in stubDir and returns the\n// path of the log every invocation is appended to.\nfunc repoCloneWriteStubGit(stubDir string) string {\n\tlogPath := filepath.Join(stubDir, \"git.log\")\n\tExpect(os.WriteFile(logPath, nil, 0o600)).To(Succeed())\n\tExpect(os.WriteFile(\n\t\tfilepath.Join(stubDir, \"git\"),\n\t\t[]byte(repoCloneStubGitScript),\n\t\t0o755,\n\t)).To(Succeed())\n\treturn logPath\n}\n```\n\nWait: `os.WriteFile(logPath, nil, 0o600)` — gosec excluded for tests, but `0o600` is fine anyway.\n\nHmm, one problem: the stub appends to `$STUB_GIT_LOG`. The child env must include it. ✓\n\nNow `repo_clone_test.go`.\n\nLet me write carefully.\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n\npackage scripts_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"io/fs\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n)\n\n// repoCloneTimeout bounds one script invocation.\nconst repoCloneTimeout = 60 * time.Second\n\n// repoCloneSandbox is the throwaway tree one spec runs the script inside.\n//\n// The script under test is a copy, so its fixed clone root is <tmp>/agent/repos\n// and a broken guard can only ever damage the temp tree.\ntype repoCloneSandbox struct {\n\trawRoot  string\n\ttmpRoot  string\n\tagentDir string\n\tscript   string\n\toutside  string\n\tstubDir  string\n\tlogPath  string\n\thome     string\n}\n```\n\nHmm, `rawRoot` — for cleanup. Since tmpRoot is EvalSymlinks(rawRoot), removing either works. Let me keep both but cleanup uses rawRoot... Actually if rawRoot is a symlinked path, RemoveAll(rawRoot) works. Use tmpRoot for clarity? EvalSymlinks output is the real path; RemoveAll on it works. Let me just keep `tmpRoot` and drop `rawRoot`. Since EvalSymlinks returns the real path, RemoveAll(tmpRoot) removes the same dir.\n\nOK, drop rawRoot.\n\nNow:\n\n```go\n// newRepoCloneSandbox builds the sandbox and copies the script into it.\nfunc newRepoCloneSandbox() *repoCloneSandbox {\n\traw, err := os.MkdirTemp(\"\", \"repo-clone-sandbox-\")\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\tresolved, err := filepath.EvalSymlinks(raw)\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\n\tsandbox := &repoCloneSandbox{tmpRoot: resolved, agentDir: filepath.Join(resolved, \"agent\")}\n\n\tscriptsDir := filepath.Join(sandbox.agentDir, \"scripts\")\n\tExpect(os.MkdirAll(scriptsDir, 0o755)).To(Succeed())\n\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(repoRoot(), \"agent\", \"scripts\", \"repo-clone.sh\"))\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\tsandbox.script = filepath.Join(scriptsDir, \"repo-clone.sh\")\n\tExpect(os.WriteFile(sandbox.script, source, 0o755)).To(Succeed())\n\n\tsandbox.outside = filepath.Join(resolved, \"outside\")\n\tExpect(os.MkdirAll(sandbox.outside, 0o755)).To(Succeed())\n\n\tsandbox.stubDir, err = os.MkdirTemp(\"\", \"repo-clone-stub-\")\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\tsandbox.logPath = repoCloneWriteStubGit(sandbox.stubDir)\n\n\tsandbox.home, err = os.MkdirTemp(\"\", \"repo-clone-home-\")\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\n\treturn sandbox\n}\n```\n\nCleanup:\n```go\n// repoCloneRemoveSandbox restores write permission, then deletes every tree the\n// spec created. Without the chmod the read-only clone would survive the run.\nfunc repoCloneRemoveSandbox(sandbox *repoCloneSandbox) {\n\tfor _, root := range []string{sandbox.tmpRoot, sandbox.stubDir, sandbox.home} {\n\t\t_ = exec.Command(\"chmod\", \"-R\", \"u+w\", root).Run()\n\t\t_ = os.RemoveAll(root)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nHmm, requirement 16: \"The tests must never create `agent/repos` in the repository itself; after `make test` it must be absent.\" Since we run the copy, ✓.\n\nroots/excludes:\n```go\n// roots returns the trees the snapshot covers.\nfunc (s *repoCloneSandbox) roots() []string {\n\treturn []string{s.tmpRoot, s.outside}\n}\n\n// reposExcludes returns the clone tree, which a successful clone is expected to change.\nfunc (s *repoCloneSandbox) reposExcludes() []string {\n\treturn []string{filepath.Join(s.agentDir, \"repos\")}\n}\n\n// dest returns the clone destination the script must resolve to.\nfunc (s *repoCloneSandbox) dest() string {\n\treturn filepath.Join(s.agentDir, \"repos\", \"bborbe\", \"foo\")\n}\n```\n\nSnapshot:\n```go\n// repoCloneSnapshot records \"path mode\" for every entry under roots, with the\n// excluded paths skipped, so a spec can assert nothing else moved.\nfunc repoCloneSnapshot(roots []string, excludes []string) string {\n\tseen := map[string]bool{}\n\tlines := []string{}\n\tfor _, root := range roots {\n\t\t_ = filepath.WalkDir(root, func(path string, entry fs.DirEntry, err error) error {\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tfor _, exclude := range excludes {\n\t\t\t\tif path == exclude {\n\t\t\t\t\tif entry.IsDir() {\n\t\t\t\t\t\treturn fs.SkipDir\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif seen[path] {\n\t\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tseen[path] = true\n\t\t\tinfo, statErr := os.Lstat(path)\n\t\t\tif statErr != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tlines = append(lines, path+\" \"+info.Mode().String())\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(lines)\n\treturn strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\")\n}\n```\n\nRun:\n```go\n// runRepoClone executes the sandboxed script through a real subprocess.\n//\n// The child environment is built explicitly: the ambient proxy variables would\n// otherwise be inherited by git, and HOME points at a scratch directory.\nfunc runRepoClone(\n\tsandbox *repoCloneSandbox,\n\tenv map[string]string,\n\targs ...string,\n) (string, string, int) {\n\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), repoCloneTimeout)\n\tdefer cancel()\n\n\tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, sandbox.script, args...)\n\tcmd.Env = []string{\n\t\t\"PATH=\" + sandbox.stubDir + string(os.PathListSeparator) + os.Getenv(\"PATH\"),\n\t\t\"HOME=\" + sandbox.home,\n\t\t\"STUB_GIT_LOG=\" + sandbox.logPath,\n\t}\n\tfor key, value := range env {\n\t\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, key+\"=\"+value)\n\t}\n\n\tvar stdout, stderr bytes.Buffer\n\tcmd.Stdout = &stdout\n\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n\n\trunErr := cmd.Run()\n\tif runErr == nil {\n\t\treturn stdout.String(), stderr.String(), 0\n\t}\n\n\tvar exitErr *exec.ExitError\n\tif !errors.As(runErr, &exitErr) {\n\t\tFail(\"run repo-clone.sh: \" + runErr.Error())\n\t}\n\treturn stdout.String(), stderr.String(), exitErr.ExitCode()\n}\n```\n\nLog helpers:\n```go\n// repoCloneLog returns everything the stub recorded.\nfunc repoCloneLog(sandbox *repoCloneSandbox) string {\n\tcontent, err := os.ReadFile(sandbox.logPath)\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\treturn string(content)\n}\n\n// repoCloneCloneLines returns only the clone invocations the stub recorded.\nfunc repoCloneCloneLines(sandbox *repoCloneSandbox) []string {\n\tall := strings.Split(repoCloneLog(sandbox), \"\\n\")\n\tlines := make([]string, 0, len(all))\n\tfor _, line := range all {\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(line, \"clone \") {\n\t\t\tlines = append(lines, line)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn lines\n}\n```\n\nAssertion helpers:\n```go\n// repoCloneExpectNotWritable asserts no entry under root carries an owner write bit.\nfunc repoCloneExpectNotWritable(root string) {\n\t_ = filepath.WalkDir(root, func(path string, _ fs.DirEntry, err error) error {\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t\tinfo, statErr := os.Lstat(path)\n\t\tExpect(statErr).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\t\tif info.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink != 0 {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t\tExpect(info.Mode().Perm()&0o200).To(BeZero(), path)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t})\n}\n```\n\nHmm — `Expect(...).To(BeZero(), path)` — Gomega's To accepts optional description. ✓\n\n```go\n// repoCloneMode returns the permission bits of path, without following symlinks.\nfunc repoCloneMode(path string) os.FileMode {\n\tinfo, err := os.Lstat(path)\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\treturn info.Mode().Perm()\n}\n\n// repoCloneIsSymlink reports whether path is itself a symbolic link.\nfunc repoCloneIsSymlink(path string) bool {\n\tinfo, err := os.Lstat(path)\n\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n\treturn info.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink != 0\n}\n```\n\nNow the specs.\n\n```go\nvar _ = Describe(\"repo-clone.sh\", func() {\n\tvar sandbox *repoCloneSandbox\n\n\tBeforeEach(func() {\n\t\tsandbox = newRepoCloneSandbox()\n\t})\n\n\tAfterEach(func() {\n\t\trepoCloneRemoveSandbox(sandbox)\n\t})\n\n\tDescribeTable(\"refuses a reference that is not owner/name\",\n\t\tfunc(ref string) {\n\t\t\tbefore := repoCloneSnapshot(sandbox.roots(), nil)\n\t\t\tstdout, stderr, exitCode := runRepoClone(sandbox, nil, \"clone\", ref)\n\n\t\t\tExpect(exitCode).To(Equal(2))\n\t\t\tExpect(stdout).To(BeEmpty())\n\t\t\tExpect(stderr).To(ContainSubstring(\"invalid repo reference\"))\n\t\t\tExpect(repoCloneLog(sandbox)).To(BeEmpty())\n\t\t\tExpect(repoCloneSnapshot(sandbox.roots(), nil)).To(Equal(before))\n\t\t},\n\t\tEntry(\"a bare name with no owner\", \"evil\"),\n\t\tEntry(\"a shell metacharacter in the owner\", \"a;b/c\"),\n\t\tEntry(\"an http scheme\", \"http://evil.example/x/y\"),\n\t\tEntry(\"a file scheme\", \"file:///etc/x\"),\n\t\tEntry(\"a leading .. segment\", \"../x\"),\n\t\tEntry(\"a trailing .. segment\", \"x/..\"),\n\t\tEntry(\"a trailing . segment\", \"x/.\"),\n\t\tEntry(\"two . segments\", \"./.\"),\n\t\tEntry(\"two .. segments\", \"../..\"),\n\t\tEntry(\"a .. owner behind the github prefix\", \"https://github.com/../x\"),\n\t\tEntry(\"a .. name behind the scp prefix\", \"git@github.com:x/...git\"),\n\t)\n```\n\nHmm — wait, \"a `..` name behind the scp prefix\": `git@github.com:x/...git` → slug `x/...git` → strip `.git` → `x/..` ✓.\n\nHmm, careful: `x/...git`. Does `${slug%.git}` remove `.git`? slug = `x/...git`. The suffix `.git` — yes, `x/..` + `.git` = `x/...git`. ✓ So slug becomes `x/..`, name = `..` ✓.\n\nNow wrong argument count:\n```go\n\tDescribeTable(\"refuses a wrong argument count\",\n\t\tfunc(args []string) {\n\t\t\tbefore := repoCloneSnapshot(sandbox.roots(), nil)\n\t\t\tstdout, stderr, exitCode := runRepoClone(sandbox, nil, args...)\n\n\t\t\tExpect(exitCode).To(Equal(2))\n\t\t\tExpect(stdout).To(BeEmpty())\n\t\t\tExpect(stderr).To(ContainSubstring(\"usage: repo-clone.sh clone <owner>/<name>\"))\n\t\t\tExpect(repoCloneLog(sandbox)).To(BeEmpty())\n\t\t\tExpect(repoCloneSnapshot(sandbox.roots(), nil)).To(Equal(before))\n\t\t},\n\t\tEntry(\"no arguments\", []string{}),\n\t\tEntry(\