": two Its ~25 lines each = ~55 lines ✓\n- \"cloning\": four Its ~22 lines each = ~95 lines ✗ too long\n\nSplit \"cloning\" into two: \"cloning\" (success + dotted) and \"re-cloning\" (second clone + failure). \n\nLet me do:\n- Describe(\"cloning into the fixed clone root\") — success It (~25 lines) + dotted It (~8 lines) = ~40 ✓\n- Describe(\"re-cloning and failure\") — second clone It (~20) + failure It (~12) = ~38 ✓\n\nGood, all under 80.\n\nHmm, but does funlen count blank lines? Default funlen counts all lines in the function body. My estimates include blanks. Should be OK.\n\nLet me be careful and keep each nested Describe compact.\n\nAlso — `BeforeEach` and `AfterEach` func literals are tiny ✓.\n\nNow let me write it.\n\nAlso I should double check: does the outer Describe's BeforeEach apply to nested Describes? Yes, Ginkgo runs outer BeforeEach before inner specs ✓.\n\nLet me write the file now.\n\nOne more consideration on `Entry` with `[]string{}` — Ginkgo DescribeTable Entry parameters: passing `[]string{}` as a single parameter to `func(args []string)` ✓.\n\nHmm, careful: Ginkgo's DescribeTable might interpret a slice parameter specially? No, it passes it as-is.\n\nLet me write.\n\nActually, for readability, instead of `func(args []string)` maybe use variadic-free explicit. Fine.\n\nLet me write the file.\n\nAlso: `Expect(os.WriteFile(...)).To(Succeed())` ✓\n\nNote on `os.Symlink(sandbox.outside, link)` — sandbox.outside is absolute ✓.\n\nLet me write it.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"128cad91-fabf-4baa-95e1-113f5b633110","uuid":"895cdadc-9589-4e6e-8a89-da2d7259e25f","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:19:08.709Z"}
