es no snapshot. The parent check is load-bearing only for the contrived shape where `<outside>/<name>` resolves back inside `repos/` — worth stating so the next reader does not assume the two specs pin the two checks independently.\n- [PROMPT] Requirement 15's **Bad subcommand** case is `log x y` — three arguments, so it exits through the argument-count branch and never reaches `[ \"$1\" != \"clone\" ]`. Requirement 2 asks for the subcommand branch to exist, so the prompt should specify `log x` (two arguments) for that entry. I kept `log x y` and added `log x` as a second entry so both branches are covered.\n- [PROMPT] Requirement 15 asks for a Go walk asserting `info.Mode().Perm()&0o200 == 0` for **every** entry, and in the same breath has the stub create `<dest>/link -> <outside dir>` inside the clone. Those are incompatible: `os.Lstat` on a symlink reports `Lrwxrwxrwx` (perm `0777`) on Linux, so the assertion fails on the link itself. The walk has to skip symlinks; the prompt should say so explicitly rather than leaving the executor to discover it from a red test.\n- [GUIDE] `go-precommit.md` should note that `gocognit` (min-complexity 20) applies to nested `filepath.WalkDir` closures in `_test.go` files. My first `repoCloneSnapshot` — a walk with an inner exclude loop, a `seen` guard and an `os.Lstat` error branch — scored 22 and failed `make lint`; extracting the exclude predicate into its own helper brought it down. The `dupl`/`errcheck`/`gosec` test exclusions in `.golangci.yml` make it easy to assume complexity linters are excluded too, but `funlen`, `gocognit` and `nestif` are not.\n- [GLOBAL] The `hideGit` note about `ROOTDIR` reads as universal but is repo-specific. Here `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` also fails, leaving `ROOTDIR` empty, yet bare `make test` and `make precommit` both succeed — `ROOTDIR` only feeds a trivy `--ignorefile` fallback in `Makefile.precommit:89`. Worth phrasing the rule as \"check whether the Makefile actually dereferences ROOTDIR\" rather than \"pass ROOTDIR to every target\", so a future run does not add an unnecessary override."}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"128cad91-fabf-4baa-95e1-113f5b633110","uuid":"735c63ec-7804-4d83-a190-9b8e2007f0de","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:24:37.290Z"}
